            <ArticleTitle>Management of opioid substitution therapy during medical intervention.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>242-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/j.1445-5994.2012.02714.x</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Opioid substitution therapy (OST) for opioid dependence is common, and injection drug users have significant medical and psychiatric comorbidity. Many physicians will encounter OST patients in their usual practice. This article provides guidance on management of common clinical problems in this population, including OST management in hepatic failure, respiratory disease, pain management and potential drug interactions.</AbstractText>
